Subject: add generic function to pmml package
Message-ID: <fI__v6qL-rE.WaXHxK_s_DcJ@rattle-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rattle-users/c/fI__v6qL-rE/m/WaXHxK_s_DcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I would like to propose to add just
this little S3 generic function to the
pmml package

pmml <- function(x, ...)
  UseMethod("pmml")

This will allow one to simply export
any model using

pmml(modelobj)

Regards,
Tobias

P.S. Example:

library(pmml)
pmml <- function(x, ...)
  UseMethod("pmml")
# kmeans example
x <- rbind(matrix(rnorm(100, sd = 0.3), ncol = 2), matrix(rnorm(100,
mean = 1, sd = 0.3), ncol = 2))
colnames(x) <- c("x", "y")
cl <- kmeans(x, 2)
pmml(cl)
# rpart example
fit <- rpart(Kyphosis ~ Age + Number + Start, data=kyphosis)
pmml(fit)

